On 6/24/07, m.kornig@sondal.net <m.kornig@sondal.net> wrote:
>
> For instance why are words like {c}, {f}, {pst}, {m}
> {kj}, {pc} or {gr} fobidden in Lojban?

{kj} is forbidden because it is a unvoiced-voiced pair. The others
are not forbidden, they are all valid cmevla.

There is an experimental cmavo {ki'ai} that would turn a cmevla
into an interjection:
<http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=ki%27ai>
Also related:
<http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=sa%27ei>

